wpa_cli: dispatch CTRL-EVENT-SSID-TEMP-DISABLED to the action script

The event dispatch in wpa_cli_action_process() has no generic fallback, so a
rejected password (reason=WRONG_KEY) never reaches an action script.  Station
mode uses that event to tell the user which saved network needs its password
re-entered.

diff --git a/wpa_supplicant/wpa_cli.c b/wpa_supplicant/wpa_cli.c
index 9bf96c4..abcacae 100644
--- a/wpa_supplicant/wpa_cli.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/wpa_cli.c
@@ -4501,6 +4501,10 @@ static void wpa_cli_action_process(const char *msg)
 		printf("wpa_supplicant is terminating - stop monitoring\n");
 		if (!reconnect)
 			wpa_cli_quit = 1;
+	} else if (str_starts(pos, "CTRL-EVENT-SSID-TEMP-DISABLED")) {
+		/* Not in the dispatch list (there is no generic fallback), so a
+		 * rejected password would never reach an action script. */
+		wpa_cli_exec(action_file, ifname, pos);
 	}
 }
 
